// std's platform layers (std/os/PLATFORM, spec §17).
// Every layer declares the same sets (fs::Error, proc::Error; spec §8, Errors, rule 14),
// so a match that lists every error a platform function may fail with checks the same on
// every platform and in the interpreter. The sets are open (rule 15): it needs `else`.
// The program builds without an error against each layer.

//# $ ctxc build linux.c {std:linux} -- main.ctx
//# exit: 0
//# exists linux.c

//# $ ctxc build macos.c {std:macos} -- main.ctx
//# exit: 0
//# exists macos.c

//# $ ctxc build windows.c {std:windows} -- main.ctx
//# exit: 0
//# exists windows.c

//# $ ctxc build interp.c {std:interp} -- main.ctx
//# exit: 0
//# exists interp.c
